**Supersedes:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), preserved unchanged.

## Context

The [re-triage of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-split) found separate parser and form-hint
paths beneath the same date symptoms. Browser-based intake guesses and matching subjects
are not sufficient evidence that two reports share one problem.

## Decision

1. Deduplicate export rows by report ID before counting.
2. Read the body and look up the tenant's locale and booking-form version.
3. Use channel plus tenant configuration to evaluate the supported cause; browser locale
   and intake tags are clues, not the source of truth.
4. Merge only reports supported by the same cause; different causes get independent tickets.
5. Unknown tenants, no matching cause, or contradictory symptoms require investigation.
   Keep their evidence visible and do not claim certainty from a classifier alone.
6. Refresh data as the desk works; distinguish report arrival from later merge activity.

## Examples and consequences

<DedupeExplorer />

Same subject does not imply same cause; different subject does not imply different cause.
Tenant lookup and body reading cost time, but avoid hiding independent fixes in one ticket.
The computed model is a triage aid, not a replacement for investigating one-day shifts.

